  "full_text": "As I walk down the highway, all I do is sing this song. And a train that's passing my way helps the rhythm move along. There is no doubt about the words are clear. The voice is strong, oh so strong. I'm just a simple guy. I live from day to day. A ray of sunshine melts the frowns and blows my blues away. There's nothing more that I can say about a day like today. I pass the time away and walk a quiet mile with you All I need from you is all your love All you gotta give to me is all your love All I need from you is all your love All you gotta give to me is all your love I'm so glad I'm leaving Gonna tell the world I am Got me a fine woman, she says I am her man One thing that I know for sure Gonna give her all my lovin' like nobody, nobody, nobody, nobody can. Standin' in the noonday sun, try to fly a ride. People go and people come to see me ride my rider by my side. It's a total disgrace to set the pace. It must be a race and the best thing I can do is run. All you gotta give to me is all your love. All I need from you is all your love. All you gotta give to me is all your love.",
